A||||5||86se/lambo||grand am brakes||||10||
Z||000000||86se/lambo||07-05-2000||10:32 PM||||maybe this is an obvious question but, what does the grand -am (late 80's)offer? bigger discs? what size? will they fit with stock wheels? vented? bigger pistons? just gotta know these things guys.thanx||||reg||10
Z||000001||vinnywolfe||07-05-2000||10:39 PM||||the 88 grand am brakes that i ended up using have a considerably bigger piston in the caliper piston.  i used the rotors off an 88 grand am also.  these vented rotors are supposedly better for heat dissipation which results in less chance of the rotor warping.  i put aftermarket 16" wheels on and everything clears just fine. my advice is to use the grand am calipers all the way around.  you will definitely notice a difference in stopping power.  if you want to take the next step, try replacing the master cylinder with one from a 94 chevy blazer.  just make sure and put your fiero master cylinder resevoir (which is lower in profile and allows for clearance when closing the hood.  do this and tell me if you don't notice the difference.<P>vinny<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||86se/lambo||07-05-2000||11:09 PM||||thanks vinny..i'm going to be using 15" wheels..think they would fit? what about the e-brake?||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||07-05-2000||11:30 PM||||The rotors are the same diameter, the difference is that they're vented (and thicker), so any stock wheel will fit. You lose the e-brake if you swap the rear brakes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||07-06-2000||12:50 AM||||I like having a working e-brake... so if/when I do this mod, I'd just do the front, and then increase the pressure to the rear brakes with an adjustable proportioning valve..<P>as well as replace the rear brakes with new Fiero rotors, and calipers, etc..<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 07-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||07-06-2000||08:59 AM||||Is'nt the sunbird rear calipers & rotors swapable? I do know that they are vented rotors w/a bigger piston and will allow you to keep the e-brake set-up.||||reg||1
